{#- Icon set, declared on every page.

  Crawlers resolve a site's favicon from the page they indexed, and until now
  only the homepage declared one — so Bing had nothing to go on for /compare/,
  /agents/ etc. and fell back to the root /favicon.ico convention, which was a
  301 to an SVG. That combination is why results rendered a blank globe.

  .ico first, SVG second: browsers prefer the typed SVG, while fetchers that
  want a raster still find one. Both are rel="icon" (not "alternate icon")
  because Google only honours icon / shortcut icon / apple-touch-icon.
  Rasters are generated by scripts/generate_favicons.py.
-#}
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
